From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 13:57:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] Typer: eqsolve (equality decision procedure) and extorder
 (order-independent extension lookup)

eqsolve decides closed equality goals with a congruence closure of the
ground equalities in scope (congruence over type constructors, and over
associated types with an abstract qualification, as in unification), and
builds a proof from reflexivity, symmetry, transitivity and the facts. It
gives up (falls back to search) when a quantified equality or a
bare-variable given is visible or the goal has open variables.

extorder: member lookup only evaluates extensions declaring the name, and
reports a lookup that depends on an extension whose extendee is being
computed as a circular extension instead of silently skipping it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011CH6tJP7hLkrpGFxEq7K6r
